1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:05,506
PC and phone memory prices were forecast to rise over 90% in three months

2
00:00:05,526 --> 00:00:08,710
Shocked by RAM prices this year?

3
00:00:08,730 --> 00:00:12,653
What AI hoovers up is HBM, next to the AI chip

4
00:00:12,673 --> 00:00:15,732
So why did PC RAM prices rise too?

5
00:00:15,752 --> 00:00:19,426
HBM needs about three times the wafers for the same amount

6
00:00:19,446 --> 00:00:21,661
That's Micron's own ratio

7
00:00:21,681 --> 00:00:26,341
A bakery using triple flour for cakes runs short of bread, so bread gets pricier

8
00:00:26,361 --> 00:00:28,215
Memory fabs are the same

9
00:00:28,235 --> 00:00:32,404
Samsung sells more of this memory than anyone

10
00:00:32,424 --> 00:00:35,473
It earned 107 trillion won in Q3 alone

11
00:00:35,493 --> 00:00:43,185
Gartner sees DRAM prices falling from late 2027; Micron says the 2028 shortage will be worse than this year's

12
00:00:43,205 --> 00:00:47,166
New fabs are coming. SK hynix's first Yongin clean room: February next year,

13
00:00:47,186 --> 00:00:51,050
Samsung's Pyeongtaek P5 aims to start in 2028

14
00:00:51,070 --> 00:00:55,437
So why did the stock fall? See the full video on YouTube
